  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3e4b5683c1ea36345958694d590b6436, type: 3}
  m_Name: COC3_Quiz_Final_Review_Q07
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::QuizQuestionData
  questionText: Everyone was removed from the printer's permissions before STUDENTS
    was granted Print. Why does the order matter?
  choices:
  - Windows requires removals before additions
  - It does not matter - the result is the same either way
  - Granting Print twice would cause an error
  - While Everyone can print, restricting the group changes nothing
  correctChoiceIndex: 3
  points: 10
  explanation: A permission granted underneath a broader one is not a restriction.
    Everyone has to go before anything you grant the group means anything.
